      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "► A significant number of people continue to describe ongoing symptoms long after the acute phase of COVID‐19, often referred to as long COVID. ► Long COVID is a heterogeneous condition with an uncertain prevalence, for which there is currently no precise case definition.",
      "reason": "Directly describes the current state of knowledge and important uncertainties about long COVID."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "This study aims to regularly synthesise evidence on long COVID characteristics, to help inform clinical management, rehabilitation strategies and interventional studies to improve long‐term outcomes.",
      "reason": "Explains the importance and need for the review by stating its purpose in informing practice and research."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Systematic reviews conducted early during the COVID‐19 pandemic soon became redundant due to the rapidity with which new research was released. We conducted a 'living' systematic review to provide frequently updated evidence on the symptoms and complications of long COVID.",
      "reason": "The need for the current review is explained due to redundancy of early reviews, but no specific previous review is identified or cited."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review is not focused on intervention effects; it is a descriptive review of long COVID characteristics."
    },
    {
